# Makery - copy to .env and edit. Nothing here is read from the repo; .env is
# gitignored, so this file is the only one that ever gets shared.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && $EDITOR .env && docker compose up -d --build
#
# Two settings have no sensible default and nothing works until both are right:
#
#   GALLERY_DIR    ComfyUI's output directory for this app. It is read
#                  directly as the gallery - nothing is copied, and there is
#                  no second source of truth.
#   NETWORK_NAME   the Docker network ComfyUI and Ollama are already on.
#                  `docker network ls`.
#
# Everything else in this file has a working default.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THE FILE IS IN THREE PARTS AND THEY ARE READ VERY DIFFERENTLY. If you only
# read one line of this header, read the one about Part 3.
#
#   PART 1 - seven that only this file can answer. Compose reads them to build
#     the container at all: the paths it mounts, the uid it runs as, the
#     network it joins, the port it publishes, what to call it. There is no
#     app yet at the moment they are read, so there is nowhere else they could
#     come from. Change one and rebuild.
#
#   PART 2 - nine that this file and the parent page share. Whatever is set on
#     the page wins; this file is the fallback and goes on applying until a box
#     on the page is filled in, and clearing that box puts this file back.
#     Nothing here is ever copied into the database, so upgrading and changing
#     nothing behaves exactly as it did before. The startup log says, for each
#     one, which of the two is in force - and never what it is.
#
#   PART 3 - seventy-four first-run defaults: everything below the big divider.
#     Each one is read ONCE, on the first start against an empty database, to
#     fill in a setting. From that moment the parent page owns it and this file
#     is never consulted for it again. EDITING ONE AFTERWARDS AND REBUILDING
#     DOES NOTHING - and the app will not tell you, because as far as it is
#     concerned you are editing a file it finished with weeks ago.
#
# So a .env with only Parts 1 and 2 in it is a complete, working configuration.
# One with only Part 1 is too.
#
# Part 3 is kept in full anyway, values and all, because it is also the list of
# what this app can be told to do - the nightly email, the weekly timetable,
# the warm-up sums, the daily limits on length - and reading it is quicker than
# booting the thing and clicking through eight tabs to find out.

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PART 1 - SEVEN THAT ONLY THIS FILE CAN ANSWER
# Compose reads these. There is nowhere else to set them. Change one, rebuild.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── where things are ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ComfyUI's output directory for this app. **Required.** ComfyUI must be
# writing here (a SaveImage/SaveVideo prefix of `makery/` lands in it),
# and this app reads it directly as the gallery - nothing is copied.
GALLERY_DIR=/srv/comfyui/output/makery

# Where the app keeps what it *decides* rather than what it makes: `state.db`
# with every parent-page setting in it, their characters, the chat transcript,
# the prompt overrides, the render timings, their banner, and the nightly
# backups. A Docker named volume by default, deliberately not inside
# GALLERY_DIR - that is ComfyUI's output directory, it is shared, and it is the
# first thing anyone wipes when a disk fills up. Put a host path here instead
# if you would rather be able to read it: STATE_VOLUME=/srv/makery
#
# If you do use a host path, make it yourself and give it to RUN_AS first -
# Docker creates a missing bind-mount source as root:root 0755, which the
# container cannot write to, and the app then quietly keeps nothing:
#
#   sudo mkdir -p /srv/makery && sudo chown 1000:1000 /srv/makery
#
# The named-volume default needs none of this: it inherits /state's own
# permissions out of the image.
STATE_VOLUME=

# ComfyUI's *input* directory. Every "Animate this" leaves a frame there that
# ComfyUI never cleans; the janitor sweeps its own `makery-*` frames (and
# `easy-iv-gen-*` from before the rename) and touches nothing else. Point it
# at ComfyUI's input dir, or leave the default to skip the sweep.
COMFY_INPUT_DIR_HOST=/srv/comfyui/input

# Who the container runs as. It has to be able to delete from GALLERY_DIR, so
# this usually wants to be a uid in the group that owns it. `id -u`, `id -g`.
RUN_AS=1000:1000

# ─── where it listens, and which network ─────────────────────────────────────

# The host port the container publishes on, for direct access and debugging.
# A proxy in front should reach the *container* port (8000) over the shared
# Docker network instead - see "Putting it behind a name" in the README.
HOST_PORT=8095
# Only matters if you run more than one of these on one machine.
CONTAINER_NAME=makery

# The Docker network ComfyUI and Ollama are already on. **Required.**
# `docker network ls` and take the full name, which is usually the directory
# their compose file lives in plus the network's own name. This compose file
# joins that network rather than making one of its own, which is what lets
# COMFY_URL and OLLAMA_URL in Part 2 be container names rather than addresses.
NETWORK_NAME=comfyui_default

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PART 2 - NINE THIS FILE AND THE PARENT PAGE SHARE
# A box filled in on the page wins. This file is the fallback, and clearing
# that box puts it back. None of these is ever copied into the database.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── the two services it talks to ────────────────────────────────────────────

# Container names on the shared Docker network named by NETWORK_NAME in Part 1,
# or host:port if you are not using one. **Both are on the page** (Settings ->
# What it talks to, and how it keeps time). A new OLLAMA_URL is used by the next
# request; a new COMFY_URL needs a restart, because the app holds one WebSocket
# open to it for progress.
COMFY_URL=http://comfyui:8188
OLLAMA_URL=http://ollama:11434

# ─── the clock, and how much it says ─────────────────────────────────────────

# The household's timezone, not the server's, if they differ: it decides when "today"
# starts, which is when the daily limits reset and the warm-up sums come back.
# **On the page**, and the one setting there that is deliberately applied only
# at startup: moving the clock under a day that is already half over would
# reset or freeze that day's allowance. So a change needs a restart.
TZ=UTC
# DEBUG is worth it once - it logs every ComfyUI message - and noisy after.
# **On the page**, and live - the next log line follows it.
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ─── the grown-up gate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The PIN on /parent. It also gates the "I'm a grown-up" box on the warm-up
# sums, and adding a profile. There is no way to switch it off: an empty value
# here means the built-in default applies, not that the gate goes away. It used
# to mean exactly that, and an unconfigured install let everybody through -
# the one setting whose unset state was the insecure one.
#
# **On the page**, under Settings -> The PIN on this page, with three rules
# that are the whole reason it took its own box rather than joining the rest:
# changing it needs the current one typed in again, it cannot be set to nothing
# (that would leave the page open), and there is no button that *removes* it.
# Three boxes ask for this PIN - the grown-up box on the sums, the parent page
# itself, and changing the PIN - and each gets its own five goes and its own
# ten minutes. Separate for two reasons: a shared count was being cleared on
# every poll of the parent page and left all of them effectively unthrottled,
# and a shared *lockout* would let a child shut their parent out of the
# settings page by getting the sums overlay wrong five times.
# A PIN somebody *types* still forgives the misses; a stored one sent by an
# open tab no longer does. /unlock on the Telegram bot clears all three. Forgotten it? See "Forgetting the PIN" in the README - it needs
# a shell on the machine, which is the point.
#
# Left blank here, and the built-in default of 1234 applies. That default is
# published in this file and in the source, so it is public knowledge: it is
# there so that a fresh install has a gate at all, not so that anybody relies
# on it. The app warns on every start until it is changed. Change it here, or
# on the parent page under Settings, before a child works out that 1234 is the
# first thing anyone tries.
PARENT_PIN=

# ─── the four credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DIGEST_SMTP_PASS and DIGEST_URL here; NOTIFY_URLS and TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN under
# the two banners after them. PARENT_PIN above is handled the same way and makes
# five. All of them are on the parent page as well, each beside the settings it
# belongs with, and all of them are handled differently from every other box
# there:
#
#   - they are **left out of the backup file**, which is the file a parent is
#     told to email to themselves. They are not rows in the settings table at
#     all; they have a store of their own that the backup skips, and a restore
#     puts the live ones back rather than clearing them.
#   - they are **never shown back** to the page. It says whether one is set and
#     where it came from, and offers Replace and Clear.
#   - they are **taken back out of every log line**, including the request URLs
#     httpx writes, which for the Telegram bot is the token itself.
#
# Whatever is in this file still applies until a box on the page is filled in.

# The password for the mail relay. Everything else about the email - the
# address, the host, the port, the sender, the subjects - is on the parent
# page, under Alerts → Daily email → Email server, and so is this, right
# underneath them. Live: the next email uses it, with no restart.
DIGEST_SMTP_PASS=

# One Apprise URL for the nightly email, used exactly as written, for a relay
# the DIGEST_SMTP_* boxes cannot describe - Gmail with an app password,
# SendGrid, SES. Filled in, it wins over all of them.
#
# It is here among the credentials rather than with the other DIGEST_* settings
# because the shape it exists for is mailtos://you:apppassword@gmail.com: a
# mail password with a hostname in front of it. It *was* an ordinary setting,
# which put that password into every backup file; an installation that already
# has one stored has it moved out of the settings on the next start, with
# nothing to do by hand. On the page, under Alerts → Daily email → Or one
# Apprise URL. Live: the next email uses it, with no restart.
#
# Not the same box as NOTIFY_URLS below. This one sends the nightly email;
# those send alerts to a phone. Neither does the other one's job.
DIGEST_URL=

# ─── messages to a phone: where they go (optional) ───────────────────────────
# Telegram, WhatsApp, Signal, ntfy, Discord and ~150 others via Apprise. One
# URL per service, space- or comma-separated. Telegram, for example:
#   NOTIFY_URLS=tgram://123456789:AA.../987654321
# https://github.com/caronc/apprise/wiki lists the URL for every service.
#
# Each place can be told what it wants, by naming events in front of it:
# made, limit, digest, flagged - plus "file" to attach the picture or video
# itself. Name nothing and that one gets everything.
#   NOTIFY_URLS="
#     made,file=tgram://123456789:AA.../987654321
#     limit,flagged=ntfy://ntfy.sh/mytopic
#   "
# That is every picture, with the file, to Telegram, and only the two worth
# interrupting someone for to the phone. *Which* events are sent at all is a
# row of switches on the parent page - and so is this, on the same card, under
# Alerts → Messages to your phone → Where they go. Live: the next message goes
# wherever it now says, with no restart.
NOTIFY_URLS=
# How big a file may be attached is on the parent page, under Alerts.

# ─── asking the bot things: the bot (optional, Telegram only) ────────────────
# The same bot can answer back: /today, /more 5, /pause, /open, /last, or a
# question in your own words, answered by Ollama from today's real numbers.
# Whether it listens at all, who may ask it and which model answers are all on
# the parent page - and so is this, on the same card. Set it only if the bot is
# not already in NOTIFY_URLS: the token inside a `tgram://` URL is the same
# token and is used automatically. Live: the bot starts listening within half a
# minute of a token appearing, with no restart.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PART 3 - FIRST-RUN DEFAULTS. THE PARENT PAGE OWNS THESE AFTER THE FIRST START.
# Nothing below this line is read again once the app has started once.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Each variable below fills in one setting, **once**, the first time the app
# starts against an empty `state.db`. From that moment the value lives in the
# database, the parent page is where it is changed, and this file is never
# consulted for it again. Editing one of these later and rebuilding changes
# nothing - which is the point: a setting that could be written from two places
# is a setting nobody can answer a question about.
#
# So there is no need to set any of them. They exist so that a fresh install
# can be handed a configuration rather than a first afternoon of clicking, and
# so an upgrade from the version that read them keeps exactly what it had.
#
# (Upgrading? Nothing to do. The old `.settings.json` is imported into the
# database on the first start and renamed to `.settings.json.migrated`, and
# anything it left to the environment picks up the value below.)

# ── who it is for ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The child's name and age, used to make the **first profile** and nothing
# else. The age is what most of the model instructions are really asking
# about, and is why what comes back reads like it was written for a capable
# reader rather than for a toddler. Leave the name empty for "My AI Factory"
# and neutral wording throughout.
#
# After the first start these belong to the profile: a name or an age is
# changed under "Who uses it" on the parent page, and the emails, the title
# and the bot all follow it from there.
#
# More than one child? There is nothing to set here either. Add them on that
# same tab - each gets their own gallery, daily limits, timetable, makers and
# age, and the app asks who is making things when it opens. The two below
# become the first profile and everything already in the gallery is theirs.
# With one person nobody ever sees a sign-in screen.
KID_NAME=
KID_AGE=

# What the whole thing is called. Blank builds it from the name above - and
# does it properly in each of the seven languages - so set this only if you
# want something other than "X's AI Factory".
APP_TITLE=

# ── which makers exist ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Turning one off takes its tab away *and* makes the routes it owns refuse, so
# reloading past it does nothing. Everything already made stays in their gallery.
# Per child, once there is more than one.
ENABLE_PICTURE=1
ENABLE_VIDEO=1
ENABLE_COMIC=1
ENABLE_MUSIC=1
ENABLE_CHAT=1
ENABLE_STORY=1

# ── when it is open ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A timetable, so it does not need closing and opening by hand twice a day.
# Outside these times they see a sign saying when it opens again, not just
# "back soon"; anything already rendering is left to finish. Empty means
# "whenever a grown-up has not closed it".
#   mon..sun, semicolons between days, commas between times on one day
#   a day with nothing after the = is shut
# e.g. OPEN_HOURS=mon=16:00-18:30;tue=16:00-18:30;wed=16:00-18:30;thu=16:00-18:30;fri=16:00-20:00;sat=09:00-12:00,14:00-20:00;sun=09:00-18:00
OPEN_HOURS=

# ── the warm-up sums ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sums before the first picture of the day, and how many. The last one is how
# long "I'm a grown-up" on that overlay lasts, in minutes.
#
# Off by default. It is a house rule rather than a safety one, so it is a thing
# a parent switches on deliberately - on the parent page under Rules -> Sums
# first, where the level and which kinds of sum are set too.
DAILY_QUIZ=0
QUIZ_QUESTIONS=3
QUIZ_BYPASS_MINUTES=60
# How hard they are:
#   easy    single digits, adding to 20, tables to 5, nothing below zero
#   medium  hundreds, tables to 12, exact division - roughly grade six
#   hard    two- and three-digit numbers, tables to 12, and some two-step sums
QUIZ_LEVEL=medium
# Which kinds they are asked, comma separated: add, sub, mul, div. At least one -
# an empty list would be a quiz they could never pass, so it falls back to all
# four. Division always comes out exact, whatever the level.
QUIZ_OPS=add,sub,mul,div

# ── the filter, and what a refusal does next ─────────────────────────────────
# Ask the vision model whether an uploaded photo is suitable for a child. Fails
# *open* if Ollama is unreachable - it is the child's own camera roll.
SCREEN_UPLOADS=1

# What happens after a refusal, beyond refusing it. The grown-ups are told
# either way, with the picture attached if there was one; this is whether the
# factory also closes until somebody opens it on the parent page.
#   (empty)  just tell me
#   photo    close if the picture checker says no to an uploaded photo
#   words    that, or anything the word filter stops
CLOSE_ON_REFUSAL=

# 1 applies the whole image-prompt blocklist to the chat, and to song lyrics,
# as well. Both off by default because that list blocks words a picture model
# cares about and a conversation does not - "blood", "gun", "beer" - so "why is
# blood red?" would be refused. See CHAT_CATEGORIES in app/chat.py and
# LYRIC_CATEGORIES in app/music.py for the shorter list that runs either way.
CHAT_STRICT=0
MUSIC_STRICT=0

# Let the parent page edit the model instructions, not just read them. Off by
# default: they are the only thing between a child and whatever the model feels
# like saying, so turning this on should be a decision.
PROMPT_EDITING=0

# ── how long things can be ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Videos, in seconds. **The one setting here where raising a number can make a
# render fail rather than just look different.** VRAM goes with pixels times
# frames: measured on a 16.3GB card, 15s at the normal quality peaks near
# 15.5GB, which is why the shipped ceiling is 15 and why *sharper* has a lower
# one of its own. A bigger card has room for more; raise it a few seconds at a
# time and watch the VRAM figure on the parent page.
VIDEO_MIN_SECONDS=5
VIDEO_MAX_SECONDS=15
VIDEO_DEFAULT_SECONDS=5
VIDEO_MAX_SECONDS_SHARP=10

# Songs, in seconds. Cheap by comparison: ACE-Step turbo runs at about 1.1
# seconds of wall clock per second of audio, and the limit is patience rather
# than memory.
MUSIC_MIN_SECONDS=10
MUSIC_MAX_SECONDS=120
MUSIC_DEFAULT_SECONDS=30

# ── tidying up ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deleted things sit in a trash for this many days before the janitor empties
# it, and frames left in ComfyUI's input directory are swept after this many
# hours. 0 on either leaves them alone.
TRASH_DAYS=7
INPUT_SWEEP_HOURS=24

# How many backup copies of the settings to keep, of each kind: the nightly
# ones, the safety copies taken before a restore, and the ones made by hand
# from the parent page. The oldest beyond this are deleted as a new one lands.
BACKUP_KEEP=7

# How many characters they may keep.
MAX_CHARACTERS=12

# ── the activity log ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What the app has done, in state.db, each entry sealed against the one before
# it so an edited or missing row shows up when you check the chain. There is no
# route in the app that deletes or shortens it; the only thing that can is the
# number below, and a trim writes its own entry saying that it ran.
#
# 0 - the default - keeps it for ever. Set a number of days only if you mean
# to forget things.
AUDIT_KEEP_DAYS=0
# Whether a refusal records the words it stopped, or only which category
# stopped them. Off: the category answers "is the filter working", and the
# sentence itself is theirs.
AUDIT_WORDS=0

# ── what new files are called ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One template per kind of thing, filled in as each file is made. Plain
# letters, numbers, dots, dashes and underscores, plus these tokens:
#
#   {date}  2026-09-16   {time} 1432   {kind} image, t2v, sticker
#   {who}   the name on the profile, slugged
#   {n}     counts up and never repeats - {n:05} pads it to 00007
#   {idea}  the first few words they asked for, slugged
#   {seed}  the number that drew it, where there is one
#
# Every pattern must contain {n} or {time}, or two files would want the same
# name. {n} is counted in state.db, not by scanning the folder the way ComfyUI
# does - which is why a delete here never hands a number back. The defaults
# below reproduce what the picture maker writes today (image_00043_.png,
# t2v_00028_.mp4). Nothing already on disk is ever renamed.
FILENAME_PICTURE={kind}_{n:05}_
FILENAME_VIDEO={kind}_{n:05}_
FILENAME_SONG={kind}_{n:05}_
FILENAME_COMIC={kind}_{n:05}_
FILENAME_FILM={kind}_{n:05}_
FILENAME_PHOTO={kind}_{n:05}_
FILENAME_STICKER={kind}_{n:05}_
FILENAME_OTHER={kind}_{n:05}_

# ── the nightly email ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 24-hour clock, local time. The limit notice is the separate "they have just run
# out for today" mail.
DIGEST_ENABLED=0
DIGEST_AT=19:30
DIGEST_MAX_ITEMS=24
DIGEST_LIMIT_NOTICE=1

# And where it goes. Nothing is sent unless DIGEST_TO and DIGEST_SMTP_HOST are
# both filled in - or DIGEST_URL is. The two credentials are **not** here: they
# are DIGEST_SMTP_PASS and DIGEST_URL, up among the credentials at the top of
# this file, and they are the parts of this that never become database rows.
# Comma-separated.
DIGEST_TO=
DIGEST_SMTP_HOST=
DIGEST_SMTP_PORT=25
DIGEST_SMTP_STARTTLS=0
# Leave empty for an unauthenticated relay.
DIGEST_SMTP_USER=
DIGEST_FROM=makery@localhost
# Blank uses the app's title / a subject built from the child's name. {date},
# {count} and {name} are filled in.
DIGEST_FROM_NAME=
DIGEST_SUBJECT=
# {things} is "pictures" or "videos".
DIGEST_LIMIT_SUBJECT=

# ── messages to a phone: which events ────────────────────────────────────────
NOTIFY_ON_MADE=0       # every picture and video as it is made
NOTIFY_ATTACH=0        # ...with the file itself attached
NOTIFY_ON_LIMIT=1      # when they run out for the day
NOTIFY_ON_DIGEST=0     # the daily summary as a message too
NOTIFY_ON_FLAGGED=1    # anything the word filter stops
NOTIFY_ON_PIN=1        # somebody getting the parent PIN wrong (email too)

# Bigger files are mentioned rather than attached. A property of the service at
# the other end - Telegram takes 50MB, most others less.
NOTIFY_MAX_MB=20

# ── asking the bot things ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Whether the Telegram bot listens as well as talks. Off by default - it is a
# way *in*, not just a way out.
TELEGRAM_ASK=0
# Who may ask it: chat IDs or @names, comma-separated. Empty means "whoever is
# in the tgram:// URL in NOTIFY_URLS", which is where these have always been
# taken from. Anyone else is ignored without a reply.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_IDS=
# How long to wait for the model answering a question.
TELEGRAM_TIMEOUT=120

# ── wording ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# en | fr | de | es | it | nl | pt. Which language the child's page opens in on
# a browser that has never chosen - and nothing more than that. Whoever is at
# the screen picks a language in their own Settings tab, and that choice lives in
# a cookie, so it wins over this from then on. The parent page stays English.
#
# Everything they read follows it: the page, the dropdowns, the closed sign,
# the progress bar, the refusals, and the helpers - "Surprise me", the chat,
# the idea writer and the lyric writer all answer in it. What the picture and
# video models are sent stays English whatever this says: they measurably do
# not understand the other six, and their words are translated on the way to
# ComfyUI.
UI_LANG=en

# ── how the helper models are held ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Ollama's keep_alive: 0 drops the model the moment it has answered, "60s" or
# "5m" keeps it resident and pays the load time once. ComfyUI and Ollama share
# one GPU here and a video render wants nearly all of it, so 0 for the idea
# helper is the safe default, and COMFY_FREE_AFTER_JOB is what makes room for
# it. The chat tab's model is bigger and is kept a few minutes so a
# back-and-forth does not reload it every turn.
SCRIPT_KEEP_ALIVE=0
CHAT_KEEP_ALIVE=5m
COMFY_FREE_AFTER_JOB=1

# What the chat helper is called, and how much of the conversation is kept for
# a parent to read. The name is a proper noun and is never translated.
CHAT_NAME=Sparky
CHAT_KEEP_MESSAGES=400

# ── which model does which job ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Three jobs, three names, and after the first start they are dropdowns on the
# parent page fed from what Ollama actually has. **This app never downloads a
# model**: a name here has to be one somebody has already `ollama pull`ed, and
# one that is not there falls back to the value below with a line in the log.
#
# The idea helper must be a **vision** model. It is handed a picture by the
# picture-aware "help me write it", by saving a character, and by the check on
# a photo they upload; a words-only model answers all three about a picture it
# was never shown.
SCRIPT_MODEL=qwen3-vl:4b-instruct
# The Chat tab. The tab hides itself if this one is not pulled.
CHAT_MODEL=gemma4:12b
# Answering your questions on Telegram. Empty means "the same as the idea
# helper", which is small and is dropped the moment it replies - a parent's
# question must not cost a render. Nothing here sees a picture, so this is the
# one of the three that may be a words-only model.
TELEGRAM_MODEL=

# she | he | they. Only used in the parent-facing text - the emails and the
# parent page - where the sentences are *about* them. Everything the child
# reads is already second person.
KID_PRONOUN=they
